      "maine_campaigns_are_10_40_period_simul": "Maine campaigns are 10–40 period simulations with do-nothing baselines, trend charts, and AI Reading. Cross-region scenarios are 4-decision self-contained learning experiences (5–10 min each) with cited regional organisations and region-specific AI disclaimers. Both count toward the mastery tiers.",
      "maine_stewardship_campaign_report": "Maine Stewardship Campaign Report",
      "mission_blurb": "Compare how ecological feedback, community trust, time horizons, and local authority shape fifteen campaigns across eleven regions.",
      "mission_label": "Systems stewardship mission",
      "mixed_results_one_bad_season_or_fundin": "Mixed results. One bad season or funding cut could reverse gains.",
      "multiregion_desc": "Complete twelve — both Maine and at least one cross-region scenario from each of the five mechanic families.",
      "no_feedback_rules_fired_or_no_log_capt": "No feedback rules fired (or no log captured).",
      "no_outcome": "No outcome",
      "no_required_order_conservation_manager": "No required order. Conservation Manager (Maine anchor) has the cleanest feedback rules for first-timers. Yellowstone Wolf Restoration is the textbook trophic cascade case study — a great first cross-region scenario after the Maine one. For shorter sessions try a cross-region scenario (5–10 min) first; for longer sessions try a Maine anchor (multi-period campaign). The strongest learning move: pair a Maine anchor with a cross-region scenario in the same mechanic family, then compare. After two completions the hub surfaces cross-campaign patterns you would not see from any single run.",
      "not_yet_earned": "Not yet earned",
      "notes_for_educators": "📝 Notes for educators",
      "open_questions_no_answer_key": "Open questions (no answer key)",
      "outbreak_response_s_equity_pho_badge_r": "Outbreak Response's equity-PHO badge requires elderly vaccination above 80 WITH maintained trust. Climate Pathway's Justice sector has the biggest feedback-rule reach across all five campaigns. In both, equity is a structural input to system performance, not a moral overlay. Watch what happens to ANY policy in either campaign when equity drops below 40.",
